# Chenevier–Lannes 2019, waves 4 to 6 (issue #1, jobs qf-chenevierlannes-s4, -s5, -s6)

Root import for `QuadFormsKB/Literature/ChenevierLannes/Wave4/`: Weyl vectors of Niemeier lattices (Propositions
3.4.2.1–3.4.2.4 and the integrality of $h$, conditional on Venkov's identity), reflections and neighbours
(Proposition 3.1.14, Lemma 3.4.2.12), and the statements of §3.4.4 (Borcherds) and of the theta filtration (§5.1).
Wave 5: heights of roots and Borcherds' inequalities (Propositions 3.4.2.8 (a), 3.4.2.9, 3.4.2.16, Theorem 3.4.2.10 (a)),
the arithmetic of the third proof of the holy constructions (Proposition 3.4.2.18), the root systems $R/2$ and the map
$\psi$ (§3.4.5, Figure 3.1), Theorem 5.2.2 (i) and proper neighbours of the Leech lattice (Corollary 5.3.2).
Wave 6: roots of the holy neighbours (Scholium 3.4.2.13, Proposition 3.4.2.14, Corollary 3.4.2.17, Proposition 3.4.3.4),
the transverse Lagrangian of $H(\mathbb{Z}/d)$ (Proposition 3.1.3), and Proposition 3.4.4.1.
Wave 7: $d$-neighbours and the lattices $\mathrm{vois}_d(L; u)$ (Propositions 3.1.4, 3.1.5) and their even unimodularity.
-/
